Hey,
I can't make any guarantees, but since in the OTB all battlers act immediately, there is a chance this would work there (I did not test anything):
To check whether all required actors are available you could try to add this to the skills note:
(Requires VisuStellas Skills&States Core)
Spoiler
JavaScript:
<JS Skill Enable>
  // Replace 3, 4 with the IDs of the participants
  let requiredActors = [3, 4].map(id => $gameActors.actor(id));
  // Make sure all participants can still act
  // (= unrestricted by states and either be the user or still be in the action queue)
  enabled = requiredActors.every(actor => {
    if (actor.isRestricted()) { return false; }
    if (!$gameParty.inBattle()) { return true; }
    if (actor === user) { return true; }
    return BattleManager._actionBattlers.includes(actor);
  });
</JS Skill Enable>
(In case this seems to work, make sure the skill is also properly disabled if some of the required actors already finished their turn)
To make sure all participating actors are losing their action (hopefully visible in OTBs turn order) when the skill is used, you could also add this to the note:
Spoiler
JavaScript:
<JS Pre-Start Action>
  // Also replace the actor IDs here:
  let requiredActors = [3, 4].map(id => $gameActors.actor(id));
  // ---
  requiredActors.reverse().forEach(actor => {
    let index = BattleManager._actionBattlers.indexOf(actor);
    if (index >= 0) {
      // Move all participants to the front of the queue:
      BattleManager._actionBattlers.copyWithin(1, 0, index);
      BattleManager._actionBattlers[0] = actor;
      // And clear their action:
      actor.clearActions();
    }
  });
</JS Pre-Start Action>
There is a chance that the moving part works, but the other actors can still input an action.
If that is the case, an easy solution might be to make a new State that lasts 0 turns and stuns the target until the end of their action, and replace the line
actor.clearActions();
with
actor.addState(27);
(replace 27 with the ID of your stun state)
